.TH DENSITY 1 "September 2026" "density 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
density \- fast lossless data compression and decompression utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B density
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILES\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B density
is an extremely fast lossless data compression utility based on Guillaume Vaudaux's
Density library. It operates using 4-byte work units and offers three distinct
algorithms (Chameleon, Cheetah, and Lion) balancing ultra-fast throughput (GB/s)
and high compression ratio.

Density files are framed in 2 MB streaming blocks protected with IEEE 802.3 CRC32
checksums, providing immediate corruption detection and full compatibility with
Unix pipelines and GNU tar.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-stdout\fR
Write output on standard output, keep original input files.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-decompress\fR
Decompress the specified files.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-test\fR
Test the integrity of compressed files using CRC32 checksums without writing to disk.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR \fIFILE\fR
Specify explicit input file path.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Specify explicit output file path.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Force overwrite of output files without prompting.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\fR
Keep (do not delete) input files during operation (default).
.TP
\fB\-1\fR, \fB\-\-chameleon\fR
Select Chameleon algorithm (fastest, dictionary lookup based, GB/s order).
.TP
\fB\-2\fR, \fB\-\-cheetah\fR
Select Cheetah algorithm (balanced speed/ratio, dual swapped dictionary + prediction, default).
.TP
\fB\-3\fR, \fB\-9\fR, \fB\-\-lion\fR, \fB\-\-best\fR
Select Lion algorithm (highest compression ratio, multi-form rank entropy).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose mode, displays compression statistics and transfer speeds.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display usage summary and exit.

.SH AUTHORS
Written by Guillaume Vaudaux (library core) and packaged for TDE / TdeZip companion tools.
